WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:04.278
A useful recommendation helps another person understand the decision,

2
00:00:04.722 --> 00:00:08.256
the people affected, the evidence and the options. It

3
00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:11.811
also makes open questions visible. Its purpose is to

4
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:15.456
support the responsible review, not to make uncertainty disappear.

5
00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.689
In the reminder example, a draft might explain why

6
00:00:19.711 --> 00:00:22.667
the team is considering a change, what is currently

7
00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.467
known, which communication methods are being compared and what

8
00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:29.222
the team still needs to learn. It should identify

9
00:00:29.244 --> 00:00:32.822
the relevant requirements and the people or offices responsible

10
00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:34.467
for reviewing the proposal.

11
00:00:35.271 --> 00:00:40.649
If participation, privacy, accessibility or feasibility questions remain open,

12
00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:43.693
name them. Do not write that people prefer a

13
00:00:43.716 --> 00:00:47.471
method unless the information supports that statement. A recommendation

14
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:50.916
can responsibly ask for further review or a limited,

15
00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:51.982
authorized test.

16
00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:55.860
Begin with the purpose and the choice that is

17
00:00:55.882 --> 00:00:59.549
still open. Then describe who may benefit or experience

18
00:00:59.571 --> 00:01:03.393
a burden and where the information came from. Distinguish

19
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:07.282
what people actually shared, what existing evidence shows and

20
00:01:07.304 --> 00:01:09.660
what the team is considering as a possibility.

21
00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:14.467
Summarize the alternatives, including the current approach when relevant.

22
00:01:15.044 --> 00:01:17.533
Describe the tradeoffs and the practical support each option

23
00:01:17.556 --> 00:01:21.911
would need. Explain why the proposed direction deserves consideration,

24
00:01:22.511 --> 00:01:26.400
and describe any remaining access, privacy, resource or implementation

25
00:01:26.422 --> 00:01:27.089
questions.

26
00:01:27.944 --> 00:01:31.300
If an option appears to reduce one barrier but

27
00:01:31.322 --> 00:01:35.656
might create another, say so. Reviewers need an honest

28
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:38.078
account of the tradeoffs, including those that may be

29
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.122
difficult to resolve.

30
00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:45.052
Identify the decision owner and any required reviewers. Depending

31
00:01:45.074 --> 00:01:48.052
on the work, this may include program leadership, policy,

32
00:01:48.186 --> 00:01:54.186
communications, accessibility, privacy, civil rights, Tribal consultation, labor relations,

33
00:01:54.319 --> 00:01:58.252
contracting or other responsible offices. Confirm what applies instead

34
00:01:58.274 --> 00:02:00.741
of treating the list as an automatic requirement for

35
00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:01.497
every decision.

36
00:02:02.308 --> 00:02:06.263
Use the current official Equity Analysis Toolkit and any

37
00:02:06.286 --> 00:02:10.352
required agency process. The One DSD resources can help

38
00:02:10.374 --> 00:02:13.174
you prepare and practice; they do not substitute for

39
00:02:13.197 --> 00:02:17.063
required approvals. A completed learning activity or worksheet does

40
00:02:17.086 --> 00:02:18.441
not authorize a change.

41
00:02:19.252 --> 00:02:23.030
If you cannot identify the appropriate reviewer, record the

42
00:02:23.052 --> 00:02:25.941
question and seek help from a supervisor or the

43
00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:29.763
responsible office. You can make a meaningful contribution by

44
00:02:29.786 --> 00:02:32.719
preparing a clear question even when someone else owns

45
00:02:32.741 --> 00:02:33.719
the final decision.

46
00:02:34.949 --> 00:02:38.192
Use words that match the actual status of the

47
00:02:38.216 --> 00:02:42.282
work. A proposed approach is proposed. An item waiting

48
00:02:42.304 --> 00:02:45.303
for review is not approved. A plan to ask

49
00:02:45.327 --> 00:02:48.192
people about an option is not evidence that people

50
00:02:48.216 --> 00:02:49.850
have already supported it.

51
00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.483
For the reminder example, a suitable next step might

52
00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.794
be to ask the responsible program and communication reviewers

53
00:02:56.817 --> 00:03:01.194
to examine requirements, participation and available methods before a

54
00:03:01.217 --> 00:03:04.217
decision. The appropriate next step in an actual case

55
00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:06.883
depends on the current process and the people authorized

56
00:03:06.906 --> 00:03:07.506
to act.

57
00:03:08.094 --> 00:03:11.672
Keep learning notes free of personal and confidential details.

58
00:03:12.094 --> 00:03:14.872
For real work, use the approved records and review

59
00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.383
channels. Follow each tool's instructions about whether a draft

60
00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:21.406
is saved, downloaded or retained only during the visit.

61
00:03:22.461 --> 00:03:25.817
In the activity below, choose the recommendation that best

62
00:03:25.839 --> 00:03:29.150
communicates what is known, what is still open and

63
00:03:29.172 --> 00:03:32.594
what review is needed. Read the feedback after choosing.

64
00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:36.017
You can compare the alternatives and revise your answer.

65
00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.504
For your own example, draft a short recommendation with

66
00:03:40.527 --> 00:03:44.349
a proposed action, the reason for considering it, one

67
00:03:44.371 --> 00:03:47.144
important uncertainty and the role that should review it.

68
00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:51.222
The next lesson begins after the appropriate people have

69
00:03:51.244 --> 00:03:55.067
authorized a change. Until then, keep the recommendation and

70
00:03:55.089 --> 00:03:59.178
any required review separate from implementation. That distinction helps

71
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.489
the work remain accountable and understandable.
